1.pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe8n5le02ob12re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "<strong>Patrick</strong>: We are gathered here today to discuss a large amount of information regarding important aspects about one of our forthcoming projects. We don't start the project next week, but next month. So, we have a lot of aspects to discuss and arrange such as the method we will use for the project's data validation. We are not arguing about a great deal of trouble with our past and current projects. Don't insist on that. Sandy, please don't focus on anything today, but on the session's minute.", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob12re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<strong>Sandy</strong>: Sure. The members of the board are discussing the proper data validation method for the project, which we don't deliver until October 4th. The challenge that the new project possesses lies in the great deal of personal data and information that we have to process and register in a large amount of paper like fields and forms. That is why the form level validation method will not be considered. Furthermore, the form level validation method is not going to be used either as its characteristics will not be suitable for the special requirements of the application. Finally, expert professionals come this afternoon to inform and formalize the final choice of implementing the data saving validation.", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob12re2img02.jpg", "time": "32000", "id": 1}, {"text": "<strong>Connor</strong>: Sandy, I don't understand what is being discussed here. Patrick doesn't explain this again this afternoon, right? <br/>\n<strong>Sandy</strong>:  No. Besides, Patrick is not explaining that to you, so let me do it. The board decided that they aren't going to implement another validation method apart from the data saving one. As the customer's expected to fill a large amount of information, this application will not save and register the customer's information until it is complete in all the different tabs. Furthermore, the application will not save the information on its own but it will have the customer press a specific button to save the information as a whole.", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob12re2img03.jpg", "time": "81000", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe8n5le02ob12re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 1, "template_override": 1}, {"type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}], "video_src": "enpe8n5le02ob12re5vsc01"}, "type": "video"}], "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 4, "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Data Validation Overview"}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you are discussing about the different validation methods to implement in future projects. "}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Designs the data structure based on the database structures and its characteristics.  Validates database using the proper IT tools."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Reads and Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.  Exchanges simple information on the data validation and data warehouses."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future With Present Simple in Negative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When we talk about future time, we usually use <i>will, going to,</i> and <i>the present continuous</i>. However, you can also use the <strong>present simple tense</strong> to refer to plans for the future."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The members of the board are discussing the proper data validation method for the project, which we don't deliver until October 4th. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We don't start the project next week, but next month."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>The <strong>present simple tense</strong> does not only refer to routines or scheduled events; in fact, it can be used to talk about <i>certain future plans</i> that are going to occur in a specific moment.&nbsp;</p> <p>Furthermore, when using this tense for future purposes, there are no significant changes in the sentence structure, you only have to include time expressions such as <i>tomorrow, next Saturday, or next month</i>, among others.</p> <p>These ideas can be expressed in both, affirmative and negative forms. Remember that when you use the <strong>present simple tense</strong> as a future, try to use <i>action verbs</i> not <i>state verbs.</i></p> <p>For example:</p> <p><i>Juan doesn&rsquo;t arrive<strong> early </strong>to the meeting <strong>tomorrow</strong>, right?</i></p> <p><i>They <strong>do not work</strong> next <strong>month.</strong></i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Patrick doesn't explain this again this afternoon, right? "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use<strong> quantifiers</strong> to determine the quantity or amount of something in an imprecise way. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>This time we are going to talk about two different <strong>quantifiers</strong> that make reference to a lot of elements.</p> <p><strong><i>A large amount of</i></strong> and <strong><i>a great deal of</i></strong> tend to report uncountable nouns. Their use is quite formal.</p> <p>&nbsp;Let&rsquo;s see some examples:</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">A Large Amount Of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\">A Great Deal Of \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <i>They will <strong>need a large amount of information</strong> to validate this project.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <i>If we use <strong>a great deal of data,</strong> we will get the results expected.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The challenge that the new project possesses lies in the great deal of personal data and information."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We are gathered here today to discuss a large amount of information regarding important aspects about one of our forthcoming projects. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We have to process and register in a large amount of paper like fields and forms. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "forthcoming"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "close to happen or occur, soon "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We are gathered here today to discuss a large amount of information regarding important aspects about one of our forthcoming projects. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob12aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "minute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a written report specifying what was discussed or decided in an important meeting"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sandy, please don't focus on anything today, but on the session's minute."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob12aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "board"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the group of people who manage a company or organization"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The members of the board are discussing the proper data validation method for the project, which we don't deliver until October 4th."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob12aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "formalize"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make a decision official and definitive"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Finally, expert professionals come this afternoon to inform and formalize the final choice of implementing the data saving validation"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob12aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tab"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "different small pieces of a system containing in each one important information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As the customer's expected to fill a large amount of information, this application will not save and register the customer's information until it is complete in all the different tabs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob12aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about data warehouses and how they are applied in the validation process. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write notes about the main features and design a poster which you describe data warehouses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your partner and answer all his questions. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I Look for information about data warehouses and how they are applied in the validation process"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write and design a poster which you describe data warehouses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about data warehouses and its features."}]}]}